Three notes. (1) `03_analyze.py` draws its bootstrap replicates from one random stream in file order, so adding a benchmark file shifts the later intervals by up to ~0.016 in the geometric-mean ratio without changing a point estimate. (2) Raw outputs (`results/raw*`) are not in git; `run_all.sh` regenerates them. (3) Thresholds and definitions (thin cell, qualifying extrapolation targets, the primary endpoint) are in `PROTOCOL.md`.
